WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:50.090 --> 00:01:56.010
<b>Godkiller</b>

3
00:01:58.750 --> 00:02:00.580
Oh, crap! He's not holding back!

4
00:02:00.580 --> 00:02:02.210
We gotta move!

5
00:02:02.210 --> 00:02:04.000
Everything here is done for!

6
00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:14.640
So, that's where those detestable Shandorian
warriors have hidden their village.

7
00:02:15.970 --> 00:02:18.510
They're originally from the Blue Sea.

8
00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:21.560
Surely they would love to go home!

9
00:02:26.170 --> 00:02:28.960
Now, fall to the world below!

10
00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:38.490
Our village, no!

11
00:02:38.490 --> 00:02:40.070
It's been destroyed!

12
00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:43.540
That could've been us.

13
00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:46.500
If we had waited any longer,
we'd be ashes.

14
00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:57.990
In the name of Great Warrior Kalgara.

15
00:03:01.330 --> 00:03:04.080
Light the fire of Shandora!

16
00:03:09.320 --> 00:03:10.450
Wyper!

17
00:03:11.170 --> 00:03:12.460
Wyper.

18
00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:15.360
Great Warrior Kalgara.

19
00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:20.420
Your distant ancestor had many reasons
for wanting to take back our homeland.

20
00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:22.540
But one you may not know.

21
00:03:22.540 --> 00:03:25.170
He had another reason?

22
00:03:25.170 --> 00:03:26.210
Yes.

23
00:03:26.210 --> 00:03:28.380
It would become his greatest regret.

24
00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:31.770
Now, listen.

25
00:03:31.970 --> 00:03:35.640
Great Warrior Kalgara
had a very close friend.

26
00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:37.180
Kalgara had a friend?

27
00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:40.980
That's right.

28
00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:45.780
He came to know Kalgara 400 years ago.

29
00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:50.110
His name... Mont Blanc Noland!

30
00:03:57.870 --> 00:04:03.500
The following tale took place long,
long ago... some 400 years in the past.

31
00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:05.340
And though it was never written down,

32
00:04:06.310 --> 00:04:10.520
it has remained in people's hearts
from one generation to the next.

33
00:04:06.350 --> 00:04:11.650
<b>Jaya, the Grand Line
400 Years Ago</b>

34
00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:15.230
Get back to the ship, quick!

35
00:04:15.230 --> 00:04:18.150
The monster of
Shandora is right behind us!

36
00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:20.480
Hurry! Cast off! Cast off!

37
00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:22.030
But Captain, there are still crewmen...

38
00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:23.650
Just get us out to sea!

39
00:04:44.180 --> 00:04:45.630
Now you'll face my wrath!

40
00:04:49.780 --> 00:04:51.280
Gah!

41
00:04:54.030 --> 00:04:55.530
Gah!

42
00:04:58.190 --> 00:05:04.080
<b>Kalgara
The Great Warrior of Shandora</b>

43
00:05:01.290 --> 00:05:02.790
Leave your possessions.

44
00:05:02.790 --> 00:05:04.750
Flee with your lives!

45
00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:18.550
<b>Elsewhere on the Grand Line...</b>

46
00:05:12.010 --> 00:05:13.970
Sir! The daily report!

47
00:05:13.970 --> 00:05:17.470
I'm sorry to inform you that we've
reached the end of our food supply.

48
00:05:17.470 --> 00:05:20.620
Meaning, of course,
we are now lost at sea.

49
00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:23.200
And will... slowly... die.

50
00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:25.620
The cook fainted!

51
00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:28.140
Dammit! No more food!

52
00:05:28.870 --> 00:05:30.460
Looks like the commodore
fell into the sea.

53
00:05:31.170 --> 00:05:32.540
This is the Grand Line!

54
00:05:32.540 --> 00:05:35.390
Did he decide to drown himself
and leave us to our fates?

55
00:05:35.390 --> 00:05:37.520
Maybe he decided on a
quick death over starvation.

56
00:05:38.350 --> 00:05:40.730
Don't be stupid!
The commodore is a great man!

57
00:05:40.730 --> 00:05:43.190
He's already returned
twice from these waters!

58
00:05:43.190 --> 00:05:46.490
Yeah! What are these carefully
folded clothes and shoes here for?

59
00:05:46.910 --> 00:05:49.040
Hey, someone go check.

60
00:05:49.040 --> 00:05:50.290
Screw that!

61
00:05:50.290 --> 00:05:51.910
This sea is chock full of monsters!

62
00:05:51.910 --> 00:05:53.370
He's not coming up.

63
00:05:54.890 --> 00:05:55.720
Commodore!

64
00:05:56.640 --> 00:05:58.260
He was a crafty one.

65
00:05:58.260 --> 00:05:59.170
Here.

66
00:05:59.170 --> 00:06:00.670
Uh, what's the rope for?

67
00:06:02.380 --> 00:06:03.750
Haul it in, boys.

68
00:06:07.010 --> 00:06:08.550
Whoa! What is that thing?

69
00:06:08.550 --> 00:06:10.890
Commodore, did you
kill that beast underwater?

70
00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:12.440
Cook it up for us.

71
00:06:12.480 --> 00:06:17.440
<b>Commodore Mont Blanc Noland
Exploration Ship
Kingdom of Lvneel, North Blue</b>

72
00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:15.310
I've been gettin' lazy. Man.

73
00:06:15.310 --> 00:06:16.980
Must be losin' my touch.

74
00:06:20.740 --> 00:06:22.930
This storm's a real whopper, Commodore!

75
00:06:22.930 --> 00:06:24.510
Ah, I've been through worse.

76
00:06:24.510 --> 00:06:26.560
What? How does that help us?

77
00:06:27.730 --> 00:06:29.810
The yardarm's been broken off!

78
00:06:29.810 --> 00:06:30.600
Where?

79
00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:31.850
Main! Main!

80
00:06:31.850 --> 00:06:36.110
This third voyage has kept
us at sea for over two years.

81
00:06:36.500 --> 00:06:39.050
And it's a miracle
we've lasted this long.

82
00:06:41.800 --> 00:06:43.630
Huh? Hey, did anybody else hear that?

83
00:06:43.970 --> 00:06:46.640
Hear what? You mean the thunder?

84
00:06:46.640 --> 00:06:48.730
No, it's something else.

85
00:06:48.730 --> 00:06:51.350
Something beautiful, like a bell.

86
00:06:49.680 --> 00:07:01.820
<b>Jaya, the Grand Line
May 21, 1222 of
the Pelagic Calendar</b>

87
00:06:54.630 --> 00:06:56.760
Priest! Are you certain of this?

88
00:06:57.050 --> 00:06:59.050
This land is cursed!

89
00:06:59.050 --> 00:07:02.270
At this rate, the Shandorians
will be wiped out!

90
00:07:02.270 --> 00:07:05.720
Then what can we
do to save the village, Priest?

91
00:07:05.720 --> 00:07:08.310
We must offer another girl.

92
00:07:10.150 --> 00:07:13.070
At the sacrificial altar!

93
00:07:21.200 --> 00:07:23.370
Too much death. How many now?

94
00:07:25.220 --> 00:07:27.180
Well over a hundred.

95
00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:29.450
How can this be?

96
00:07:29.930 --> 00:07:32.350
Nothing like this
has ever happened to us.

97
00:07:37.310 --> 00:07:40.770
If I can help save the village,
then I will gladly sacrifice my life.

98
00:07:43.820 --> 00:07:45.820
Why do you cry? Mother.

99
00:07:46.850 --> 00:07:52.270
It is truly an honor to be chosen as
sacrifice and embraced by the Sun God.

100
00:07:52.270 --> 00:07:56.900
Today is a proud and happy day for me,
and it should be for you as well.

101
00:08:00.540 --> 00:08:04.130
Thank you so much for raising
me right these many years, Mama.

102
00:08:04.800 --> 00:08:06.300
Mousse!

103
00:08:10.300 --> 00:08:13.010
If this is a bad dream, let me wake up!

104
00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:17.590
Get off of me! Get off!

105
00:08:17.590 --> 00:08:19.340
Go away!

106
00:08:23.070 --> 00:08:24.940
Great Warrior Kalgara.

107
00:08:25.360 --> 00:08:26.990
Seto.

108
00:08:26.990 --> 00:08:30.360
I wanted to grow up
to be just like you someday.

109
00:08:30.590 --> 00:08:34.340
I wanted to be a brave warrior
and fight to protect this land!

110
00:08:38.300 --> 00:08:41.140
I don't wanna die from
something like this!

111
00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:49.330
You're amazing, Commodore!

112
00:08:49.330 --> 00:08:53.290
We took the heading you said to,
and sure enough, there's an island!

113
00:08:53.290 --> 00:08:54.750
Yes, how fortunate.

114
00:08:54.750 --> 00:08:57.020
We can ride out the storm here.

115
00:08:57.020 --> 00:08:59.360
Still, you sure none
of you guys heard it?

116
00:08:59.360 --> 00:09:00.650
Nope.

117
00:09:00.650 --> 00:09:02.610
None of us heard any bells.
Isn't that right?

118
00:09:02.610 --> 00:09:03.730
Yeah!

119
00:09:03.730 --> 00:09:05.480
You must've been hearing
things, Commodore.

120
00:09:13.230 --> 00:09:14.600
That's quite a forest.

121
00:09:15.580 --> 00:09:18.160
I hope we find
stuff to help our research.

122
00:09:26.030 --> 00:09:28.490
Hey, Commodore! There's your bell!

123
00:09:28.490 --> 00:09:30.120
All right, enough, boys.

124
00:09:30.120 --> 00:09:31.410
No need to tease.

125
00:09:33.080 --> 00:09:36.660
Do you really think I'd mistake
that freak bird call for a bell?

126
00:09:38.490 --> 00:09:40.120
Wait, Commodore. Did you...?

127
00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:04.730
It's unreal.
It has such a beautiful tone.

128
00:10:06.420 --> 00:10:08.550
Seems there are people here after all.

129
00:10:10.110 --> 00:10:12.650
Hey, Commodore, slow down! Wait for us!

130
00:10:16.780 --> 00:10:18.950
Someone's collapsed over here!

131
00:10:19.690 --> 00:10:21.780
Intruders.

132
00:10:23.680 --> 00:10:25.010
Hey! You there!

133
00:10:25.010 --> 00:10:26.510
Commodore!

134
00:10:26.510 --> 00:10:27.850
He doesn't look right!

135
00:10:29.700 --> 00:10:30.860
Get back here!

136
00:10:32.400 --> 00:10:34.110
Let me go!

137
00:10:36.210 --> 00:10:37.970
It's a plague called "tree fever."

138
00:10:37.970 --> 00:10:40.010
From the looks of him,
he hasn't been treated.

139
00:10:40.010 --> 00:10:42.550
What are we waiting for? Let's go!

140
00:10:42.550 --> 00:10:44.620
Doctor, check our Conine stores.

141
00:10:44.620 --> 00:10:47.790
Administer doses to this young
man and the crew immediately.

142
00:10:53.550 --> 00:10:54.800
This is terrible.

143
00:10:55.050 --> 00:10:57.310
Even the crops are being eaten away.

144
00:11:01.060 --> 00:11:03.440
Commodore!
The whole village is infected!

145
00:11:15.240 --> 00:11:17.780
Bring the girl to the altar!

146
00:11:21.370 --> 00:11:23.410
God of the sun!

147
00:11:23.410 --> 00:11:24.790
God of the rain!

148
00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:28.580
God of the forest!

149
00:11:29.130 --> 00:11:31.420
God of the earth!

150
00:11:32.040 --> 00:11:36.590
In exchange for this girl's
life, we beseech you.

151
00:11:36.590 --> 00:11:38.220
Spare our village!

152
00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:52.730
It's the Kashi God!

153
00:11:56.980 --> 00:11:58.130
Mousse!

154
00:11:58.130 --> 00:12:00.550
For the village. Let her go!

155
00:12:01.360 --> 00:12:02.820
The Kashi God.

156
00:12:02.820 --> 00:12:04.660
Such a divine form!

157
00:12:07.460 --> 00:12:09.170
Please save my mother.

158
00:12:10.120 --> 00:12:11.830
Please save my son.

159
00:12:11.830 --> 00:12:13.620
And spare my father.

160
00:12:15.380 --> 00:12:17.340
What's that? Something fell in!

161
00:12:17.460 --> 00:12:18.580
Fell in?

162
00:12:36.200 --> 00:12:37.370
Wh-What just happened?

163
00:12:38.150 --> 00:12:39.400
Who is that?

164
00:12:39.400 --> 00:12:40.740
Kashi, no!

165
00:12:40.740 --> 00:12:42.030
He's killed a God!

166
00:12:48.540 --> 00:12:50.290
The ceremony is over.

167
00:12:50.670 --> 00:12:52.290
You must've been frightened.

168
00:12:52.290 --> 00:12:53.670
But you're safe now.

169
00:12:53.670 --> 00:12:55.670
There's no need to die.

170
00:12:59.130 --> 00:13:01.550
Kashi, please forgive us!

171
00:13:01.550 --> 00:13:03.510
We're all going to be cursed!

172
00:13:03.510 --> 00:13:04.350
Kill them both!

173
00:13:04.350 --> 00:13:08.020
Offer the gods more lives
before we incur their wrath!

174
00:13:08.210 --> 00:13:10.050
Kalgara! Kill them!

175
00:13:10.050 --> 00:13:12.590
The commodore's
gone and done it this time!

176
00:13:12.590 --> 00:13:14.510
They sound really mad!

177
00:13:14.510 --> 00:13:17.090
That guy can't just keep to himself!

178
00:13:17.090 --> 00:13:18.500
He killed a god?

179
00:13:18.500 --> 00:13:20.090
What does that mean?

180
00:13:20.090 --> 00:13:23.590
Tribal rituals ain't
something you mess around with!

181
00:13:23.590 --> 00:13:26.800
Quell the gods'
anger, Great Warrior Kalgara!

182
00:13:26.800 --> 00:13:29.180
I am an explorer from the North Blue!

183
00:13:29.180 --> 00:13:30.610
Commodore Mont Blanc Nol...

184
00:13:30.610 --> 00:13:32.940
I don't care who you are, outsider!

185
00:13:33.580 --> 00:13:34.880
You must be eliminated!

186
00:13:35.780 --> 00:13:37.740
Eliminated? Is that your answer?

187
00:13:37.740 --> 00:13:40.460
You just destroy all
manner of progress?

188
00:13:40.460 --> 00:13:42.880
You have no right
to impose your values!

189
00:13:42.880 --> 00:13:44.840
Now. Say goodbye!

190
00:13:45.350 --> 00:13:46.810
Who is this guy?

191
00:13:46.810 --> 00:13:48.720
He's holding his own against Kalgara!

192
00:13:55.510 --> 00:13:56.760
Girl!

193
00:13:56.760 --> 00:13:59.470
Use that blade to give
your life to the gods!

194
00:14:01.820 --> 00:14:02.950
Do what?

195
00:14:02.950 --> 00:14:07.370
A sacrifice meant to save the entire village,
weeping because she wants to live?

196
00:14:07.370 --> 00:14:08.790
Disgraceful!

197
00:14:12.870 --> 00:14:14.250
Don't be a fool!

198
00:14:16.210 --> 00:14:16.960
Stop!

199
00:14:32.600 --> 00:14:34.980
Commodore, no!

200
00:14:39.440 --> 00:14:43.150
For centuries, our people have strictly
upheld the sacred commandment...

201
00:14:43.150 --> 00:14:45.790
that all intruders on
this island must be punished.

202
00:14:45.790 --> 00:14:49.500
And you have commited the unforgivable
sin of slaughtering Kashi.

203
00:14:49.500 --> 00:14:51.280
You alone cannot atone for that.

204
00:14:51.280 --> 00:14:54.620
You and all your men
will pay with your lives!

205
00:14:54.620 --> 00:14:56.300
"Sacrifices" this.

206
00:14:56.300 --> 00:14:57.550
"Lives" that.

207
00:14:57.550 --> 00:14:58.760
It's insane!

208
00:14:58.760 --> 00:15:01.100
How does that make your gods happy?

209
00:15:01.100 --> 00:15:06.140
These ceremonies are flat-out denials
of the triumphs of all great men before us.

210
00:15:06.140 --> 00:15:08.190
I won't stand for it!

211
00:15:08.190 --> 00:15:11.020
You insult every
adventurer and researcher

212
00:15:11.020 --> 00:15:15.990
who's ever set out to sea in hopes
of bringing prosperity to mankind!

213
00:15:15.990 --> 00:15:17.970
How shameful!

214
00:15:18.400 --> 00:15:21.190
If your gods value your lives,

215
00:15:21.190 --> 00:15:25.360
wouldn't they have contempt
for these very ceremonies?

216
00:15:28.740 --> 00:15:30.200
Give me some time, people.

217
00:15:32.360 --> 00:15:34.030
Your so-called curse?

218
00:15:34.030 --> 00:15:36.240
I will lift it for good.

219
00:15:36.240 --> 00:15:37.910
And if I cannot...

220
00:15:37.910 --> 00:15:40.860
You may do what you
will with my crew and I.

221
00:15:42.320 --> 00:15:44.780
What nonsense!
Do you think you're a god?

222
00:15:46.990 --> 00:15:48.690
And in return...

223
00:15:48.690 --> 00:15:51.500
If I do save this
village from tragedy...

224
00:15:51.500 --> 00:15:55.130
You must swear never to
perform this ceremony again!

225
00:15:55.400 --> 00:15:57.880
Is that all you have to say?

226
00:15:57.880 --> 00:16:01.010
Ridiculous! Now prepare to die!

227
00:16:01.010 --> 00:16:02.510
Let him try!

228
00:16:03.710 --> 00:16:04.880
What're you saying?

229
00:16:04.880 --> 00:16:05.930
Chief, no!

230
00:16:07.090 --> 00:16:09.510
You will have until sundown tomorrow.

231
00:16:09.510 --> 00:16:11.640
When your crew will die.

232
00:16:11.640 --> 00:16:13.430
I accept your terms.

233
00:16:16.190 --> 00:16:17.850
Aww...

234
00:16:17.850 --> 00:16:23.200
Well, fellas, come sunset tomorrow,
it looks like it's "goodbye world" for us!

235
00:16:23.530 --> 00:16:24.900
Have faith in the commodore.

236
00:16:25.680 --> 00:16:27.100
Hey, pretty lady!

237
00:16:27.100 --> 00:16:30.930
I feel bad for you too.
It's a shame you were born here.

238
00:16:31.890 --> 00:16:34.680
Yeah! With your looks, you could've married
an aristocrat and lived the good life!

239
00:16:34.910 --> 00:16:36.000
Knock it off, guys!

240
00:16:36.000 --> 00:16:37.370
Learn a little tact!

241
00:16:37.770 --> 00:16:38.560
Who is he?

242
00:16:39.310 --> 00:16:41.480
Huh? Who? You mean the commodore?

243
00:16:41.480 --> 00:16:43.360
His name is Mont Blanc Noland.

244
00:16:43.770 --> 00:16:46.220
He's a rather famous explorer.

245
00:16:46.220 --> 00:16:47.890
He's also a skilled botanist.

246
00:16:47.890 --> 00:16:52.850
He explores uncharted islands and documents
new species of plants for his research.

247
00:16:52.850 --> 00:16:55.490
He's pretty much a hero in our country.

248
00:16:55.490 --> 00:16:57.740
But he's way too nice a guy!

249
00:16:57.740 --> 00:17:01.090
Yeah, it's impossible for him
to ignore a situation like this!

250
00:17:01.090 --> 00:17:02.970
We know we can trust him though!

251
00:17:05.380 --> 00:17:08.630
Why did you not
let Kalgara kill him right then?

252
00:17:08.630 --> 00:17:11.720
The answer will
make itself known tomorrow.

253
00:17:11.720 --> 00:17:14.220
He says he can save our village.

254
00:17:14.220 --> 00:17:16.140
There is no harm in waiting.

255
00:17:16.140 --> 00:17:17.890
How can you be so sure?

256
00:17:17.890 --> 00:17:22.100
You'll listen to him,
but not the shaman's dying words?

257
00:17:22.480 --> 00:17:25.570
Kalgara! Please say something
about this outrage!

258
00:17:25.570 --> 00:17:28.280
If I sense that the village is
in even the slightest danger,

259
00:17:28.280 --> 00:17:32.950
I will not hesitate to take that
man's head before sunset tomorrow.

260
00:17:33.950 --> 00:17:37.370
I may not have the power
to hear the words of the gods.

261
00:17:37.950 --> 00:17:38.790
However...

262
00:17:39.540 --> 00:17:44.280
I can hear the words of a man
who speaks in earnest.

263
00:17:44.280 --> 00:17:45.840
Now, that is all.

264
00:17:46.510 --> 00:17:47.510
Hmph.

265
00:17:51.060 --> 00:17:52.690
What are you still doing awake?

266
00:17:53.050 --> 00:17:53.840
I'm all better.

267
00:17:55.930 --> 00:17:58.020
Great Warrior Kalgara.

268
00:17:58.770 --> 00:18:02.060
What did he mean? By "progress?"

269
00:18:12.280 --> 00:18:14.200
Here we are! A Cona tree!

270
00:18:14.550 --> 00:18:16.590
I knew there had to be one.

271
00:18:16.590 --> 00:18:18.340
In a forest this huge?

272
00:18:18.700 --> 00:18:24.710
<b>Dawn</b>

273
00:18:24.000 --> 00:18:25.830
Earthquake!

274
00:18:26.070 --> 00:18:27.240
It's here!

275
00:18:27.240 --> 00:18:29.530
Kashi's wrath has finally come!

276
00:18:33.360 --> 00:18:35.740
Let us out of here, please!

277
00:18:47.410 --> 00:18:49.540
Such devastation.

278
00:18:49.540 --> 00:18:51.790
The forest floor has sunk.

279
00:18:51.790 --> 00:18:54.670
It looks as if the island
is tearing itself apart.

280
00:19:02.300 --> 00:19:04.890
You're looking well.

281
00:19:06.180 --> 00:19:10.850
I suppose the gods have taken your
punishment into their own divine hands.

282
00:19:12.770 --> 00:19:16.690
Then your gods... have grown weak.

283
00:19:16.690 --> 00:19:22.700
They lack... the strength
to kill even one lowly explorer.

284
00:19:25.660 --> 00:19:27.530
Stubborn fool!

285
00:19:27.530 --> 00:19:30.450
Sorry, but would you mind leaving?

286
00:19:30.450 --> 00:19:32.670
I don't feel like looking at you.

287
00:19:32.690 --> 00:19:36.200
I have to... hurry to the village.

288
00:19:36.260 --> 00:19:38.090
How amusing.

289
00:19:38.090 --> 00:19:40.300
I'll enjoy watching this.

290
00:19:40.300 --> 00:19:42.050
Go ahead and squirm!

291
00:19:43.980 --> 00:19:45.940
Another warrior has died.

292
00:19:47.580 --> 00:19:49.580
And there was that terrible earthquake.

293
00:19:55.120 --> 00:19:57.160
You are the evil spirits!

294
00:19:57.160 --> 00:19:59.570
Now we will punish you!

295
00:19:59.570 --> 00:20:00.990
This wasn't the agreement!

296
00:20:01.560 --> 00:20:02.180
– Look out!
– Stop!

297
00:20:08.750 --> 00:20:10.830
Seto! Move aside!

298
00:20:10.830 --> 00:20:12.000
What's the meaning of this?

299
00:20:12.000 --> 00:20:13.250
This is pathetic.

300
00:20:13.250 --> 00:20:16.840
The Shandoran warriors
I know and look up to...

301
00:20:16.840 --> 00:20:20.090
They show a lot more pride than you do.

302
00:20:20.090 --> 00:20:21.590
Kid...

303
00:20:21.900 --> 00:20:23.860
It won't be long now.

304
00:20:23.860 --> 00:20:26.740
You should prepare yourself
for when the sun sets.

305
00:20:27.330 --> 00:20:32.380
That's when the lives of your men...
will be an offering... unto the gods.

306
00:20:40.510 --> 00:20:41.520
Dammit!

307
00:20:45.560 --> 00:20:46.900
My...

308
00:20:46.900 --> 00:20:49.900
The earth certainly did
swallow you up skillfully.

309
00:20:49.900 --> 00:20:52.070
It was truly an act of god!

310
00:20:52.070 --> 00:20:55.200
The fact that you're still alive
is what's hardest to believe!

311
00:21:20.880 --> 00:21:22.590
Prepare for the ceremony!

312
00:21:22.590 --> 00:21:25.060
Bring every sacrifice to the altar!

313
00:21:25.470 --> 00:21:26.890
Please, wait a little longer!

314
00:21:27.100 --> 00:21:29.310
The commodore'll
be back in a few more hours!

315
00:21:29.310 --> 00:21:30.930
Give us more time! Please!

316
00:21:30.930 --> 00:21:32.600
Why are they doing this to us?

317
00:21:34.900 --> 00:21:36.610
The sun is setting.

318
00:21:36.610 --> 00:21:38.610
The ceremony must be starting soon.

319
00:21:42.960 --> 00:21:44.630
How disgusting.

320
00:21:44.630 --> 00:21:48.300
Is this the wreck of a man
who defied the gods?

321
00:21:48.300 --> 00:21:51.310
What exactly are you so afraid of?

322
00:21:51.310 --> 00:21:52.010
Afraid?

323
00:21:52.010 --> 00:21:53.850
You fear what you do not know!

324
00:21:54.550 --> 00:21:58.390
And you trade innocent people's
lives for false consolations!

325
00:21:58.390 --> 00:22:00.600
What are you saying?

326
00:22:00.600 --> 00:22:03.410
Sacrifices... are pointless deaths!

327
00:22:09.370 --> 00:22:12.540
We have lived this way for centuries!

328
00:22:13.380 --> 00:22:16.090
That doesn't make it right!

329
00:22:16.090 --> 00:22:17.550
Silence!

330
00:22:17.550 --> 00:22:19.960
You don't know what
you're talking about!

331
00:22:20.660 --> 00:22:23.850
The lives of your citizens
are more precious than gods.

332
00:22:26.600 --> 00:22:28.140
They're real people!

333
00:22:31.250 --> 00:22:33.420
Take the sacrifices to the altar!

334
00:22:33.420 --> 00:22:36.590
Burn them at the stake and
send them to the Heavens!

335
00:22:41.880 --> 00:22:43.920
Commodore! Don't let them burn us!

336
00:22:48.530 --> 00:22:53.280
You can send an
innocent girl to her death.

337
00:22:53.560 --> 00:22:57.480
And have no remorse, so I doubt
you'd understand, but try.

338
00:22:57.640 --> 00:22:59.850
What you're doing is less than human!

339
00:22:59.850 --> 00:23:01.230
Don't you see that?

340
00:23:04.610 --> 00:23:06.520
No remorse, you say.

341
00:23:07.880 --> 00:23:10.380
The innocent girl you speak of.

342
00:23:12.830 --> 00:23:14.660
She was my daughter!

343
00:23:16.820 --> 00:23:17.520
What?

344
00:23:17.520 --> 00:23:20.480
You would tell your own
daughter to give up her life?

345
00:23:21.600 --> 00:23:24.310
You're very wrong.
And you don't understand.

346
00:23:24.310 --> 00:23:27.020
There is so much power
in the words of our gods.

347
00:23:27.020 --> 00:23:29.800
And the people must obey.

348
00:23:29.800 --> 00:23:32.530
The gods will not hear our pleas!

349
00:23:32.530 --> 00:23:35.780
Even if we ask them
to spare our children.

350
00:23:42.920 --> 00:23:44.670
It's smaller than the last one.

351
00:23:44.670 --> 00:23:47.720
It must be one of Kashi's children!

352
00:23:47.860 --> 00:23:51.450
The gods' blood has come
to pass judgment on you!

353
00:23:51.800 --> 00:23:54.100
Judgment my ass!

354
00:23:56.490 --> 00:23:57.820
Let me explain.

355
00:23:57.820 --> 00:23:59.280
Tree Fever is a plague.

356
00:23:59.280 --> 00:24:01.710
A plague that wiped out
hundreds of thousands of lives

357
00:24:01.710 --> 00:24:04.880
in my own village years ago
and now it is ravaging yours.

358
00:24:04.880 --> 00:24:06.050
But it's gone.

359
00:24:06.050 --> 00:24:11.740
No one's died in decades as a result
of this awful disease. No one!

360
00:24:11.740 --> 00:24:14.660
And do you know why?

361
00:24:14.890 --> 00:24:18.140
Because we discovered a cure for it!

362
00:24:19.060 --> 00:24:22.650
I'm holding in my hand
bark from the Cona tree.

363
00:24:23.250 --> 00:24:24.670
This is the cure!

364
00:24:24.670 --> 00:24:27.670
I only need to extract
the Conine from it!

365
00:24:27.670 --> 00:24:32.390
If I can bring this back to your people,
I can save all of their lives!

366
00:24:35.600 --> 00:24:39.440
But you insist on keeping
countless masses from their cure.

367
00:24:39.440 --> 00:24:43.780
Do you realize how many innocent victims
have already perished because of you?

368
00:24:44.900 --> 00:24:46.940
So I stand by what I said.

369
00:24:46.940 --> 00:24:50.240
Your ceremonies are
an insult to my people.

370
00:24:50.240 --> 00:24:52.490
You're too busy blindly trampling over

371
00:24:52.490 --> 00:24:55.540
great advancements to see how
much it could benefit you!

372
00:24:57.310 --> 00:25:00.980
I may die in judgment,
or I may die in an accident.

373
00:25:01.250 --> 00:25:03.500
At least I'll stay true to my people.

374
00:25:04.250 --> 00:25:06.830
How will your village die,
by ignorance?

375
00:25:06.830 --> 00:25:11.540
Is the pain you cause your people
worth it to be true to your Gods?

376
00:25:15.840 --> 00:25:17.790
This is a man who speaks earnest words.

377
00:25:17.790 --> 00:25:18.960
I recognize that.

378
00:25:22.380 --> 00:25:23.670
Answer this.

379
00:25:25.800 --> 00:25:28.220
What is this thing?

380
00:25:28.220 --> 00:25:29.680
What have I killed?

381
00:25:30.380 --> 00:25:32.720
– A snake.
– No!

382
00:25:32.720 --> 00:25:33.520
You're wrong!

383
00:25:33.520 --> 00:25:36.900
I just broke one of our commandments!

384
00:25:37.680 --> 00:25:41.180
I just killed a precious god!

385
00:25:41.180 --> 00:25:44.270
A god! Do you understand me?

386
00:25:48.690 --> 00:25:51.060
But all you can see is a snake!

387
00:25:51.060 --> 00:25:54.400
And you see our deadly curse
as some curable disease!

388
00:25:54.400 --> 00:25:56.690
Tell me! Can you save our village?

389
00:25:57.700 --> 00:25:59.000
I can.

390
00:27:11.710 --> 00:27:17.230
When you're lost and alone, call out and lead me to your side

391
00:27:17.450 --> 00:27:22.650
As you wander far from home, you search the sky and never hide

392
00:27:22.650 --> 00:27:25.450
You are so much like the moon

393
00:27:25.450 --> 00:27:30.100
Calmer than a star, your twinkling's lost

394
00:27:33.550 --> 00:27:42.500
A deep reflection shines, you slowly leave, fading, and what's the cost?

395
00:27:42.560 --> 00:27:47.730
Stay as you are, don't lose your way

396
00:27:47.730 --> 00:27:56.040
Let my words guide you, and look ahead until the day!

397
00:27:56.680 --> 00:28:02.930
Don't give up on your dreams, through endless nights they come to you

398
00:28:02.930 --> 00:28:08.550
If you stop, you'll never see them shining through!

399
00:28:09.790 --> 00:28:14.320
Will you return? Maybe not... Will you learn? I hope you do

400
00:28:14.320 --> 00:28:20.710
Please put your past to rest, and live your life anew.
